  "body": "I'd like to see `URL` objects' main data properties all become owned properties (or at least enumerable), i.e. `origin`, `protocol`, `username`, `password`, `host`, `hostname`, `port`, `pathname`, `search`, `hash`, and maybe `href` and `searchParams`.\r\n\r\nWithout that nature, it makes these `URL` objects extremely frustrating to work with as they do not fit well semantically in normal object models due to their lack of owned properties, e.g. when comparing 2 `URL` objects:\r\n - https://github.com/JamesMGreene/chai-deep-match/issues/2\r\n - https://github.com/lodash/lodash/issues/3121\r\n - https://github.com/debitoor/chai-subset/issues/60\r\n",
